window.QBANK = window.QBANK || {};
window.QBANK["sma-bahasa-inggris"] = {
  level: "SMA", subject: "Bahasa Inggris", duration: 900,
  questions: [
    { q: "She ___ to school every day.", options: ["go", "goes", "going", "gone"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: subjeknya she, yaitu orang ketiga tunggal. Langkah 2: kalimat menyatakan kebiasaan (every day), jadi memakai simple present tense. Langkah 3: pada simple present, verb untuk subjek orang ketiga tunggal ditambah s/es, sehingga go menjadi goes." },
    { q: "They ___ football yesterday.", options: ["play", "plays", "played", "playing"], answer: 2, solution: "Langkah 1: ada penanda waktu yesterday yang menunjukkan kejadian lampau. Langkah 2: untuk kejadian lampau memakai simple past tense. Langkah 3: bentuk past dari play adalah played." },
    { q: "Read the text: Dina wakes up at 5 a.m. every day. She helps her mother cook breakfast, then she goes to school by bicycle. She never arrives late. How does Dina go to school?", options: ["By bicycle", "By bus", "On foot", "By car"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: baca teks dengan saksama. Langkah 2: temukan informasi cara Dina ke sekolah pada kalimat she goes to school by bicycle. Langkah 3: jadi Dina pergi ke sekolah dengan sepeda (by bicycle)." },
    { q: "The cake ___ by my mother this morning.", options: ["baked", "is bake", "bakes", "was baked"], answer: 3, solution: "Langkah 1: subjek the cake dikenai perbuatan, jadi kalimatnya pasif. Langkah 2: penanda waktu this morning menunjukkan lampau, jadi memakai was/were + verb-3. Langkah 3: bentuk yang tepat adalah was baked." },
    { q: "This book is ___ than that one.", options: ["interesting", "more interesting", "most interesting", "interestinger"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: ada kata than yang menandakan perbandingan comparative. Langkah 2: kata sifat yang terdiri dari tiga suku kata atau lebih memakai more di depannya. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah more interesting." },
    { q: "I have ___ in Jakarta since 2020.", options: ["live", "lives", "lived", "living"], answer: 2, solution: "Langkah 1: pola have + since 2020 menunjukkan present perfect tense. Langkah 2: present perfect memakai have/has + verb-3. Langkah 3: bentuk verb-3 dari live adalah lived." },
    { q: "There ___ many students in the library.", options: ["are", "is", "was", "be"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: perhatikan subjeknya, many students yang berbentuk jamak. Langkah 2: pada pola there + be, bentuk be mengikuti jumlah subjeknya. Langkah 3: karena subjek jamak dan waktunya sekarang, dipakai are." },
    { q: "The synonym of happy is ...", options: ["sad", "angry", "tired", "glad"], answer: 3, solution: "Langkah 1: happy artinya senang atau bahagia. Langkah 2: sinonim adalah kata yang maknanya sama atau mirip. Langkah 3: glad berarti senang/gembira, sehingga menjadi sinonim yang tepat." },
    { q: "If it rains tomorrow, we ___ at home.", options: ["stay", "will stay", "stayed", "would stay"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: pola If + present tense menunjukkan conditional sentence type 1 (kemungkinan nyata di masa depan). Langkah 2: pada type 1, induk kalimat memakai will + verb-1. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah will stay." },
    { q: "Read the text: Rudi studied hard for the math test. He practiced 20 problems every night for a week. What can we conclude about Rudi?", options: ["He is lazy", "He hates math", "He is diligent", "He failed the test"], answer: 2, solution: "Langkah 1: perhatikan fakta di teks, Rudi berlatih 20 soal setiap malam selama seminggu. Langkah 2: perilaku tersebut menunjukkan usaha yang tekun dan rajin. Langkah 3: kesimpulan yang tepat adalah Rudi rajin (diligent)." },
    { q: "In a narrative text, the part that introduces the characters and the setting is called ...", options: ["complication", "orientation", "resolution", "coda"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: ingat struktur teks naratif: orientation, complication, resolution, (coda). Langkah 2: orientation berfungsi memperkenalkan tokoh, latar tempat, dan latar waktu cerita. Langkah 3: jadi jawabannya orientation." },
    { q: "The final part of an analytical exposition text, which restates the writer's position, is called ...", options: ["thesis", "argument", "orientation", "reiteration"], answer: 3, solution: "Langkah 1: ingat struktur analytical exposition: thesis, arguments, reiteration. Langkah 2: reiteration adalah penegasan ulang posisi penulis di akhir teks. Langkah 3: jadi jawabannya reiteration." },
    { q: "Unlike analytical exposition, a hortatory exposition text ends with a ...", options: ["recommendation", "reiteration", "complication", "resolution"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: hortatory exposition bertujuan membujuk pembaca untuk melakukan sesuatu. Langkah 2: karena itu bagian akhirnya berisi saran atau anjuran (recommendation), bukan sekadar penegasan ulang. Langkah 3: jadi jawabannya recommendation." },
    { q: "English ___ in many countries around the world.", options: ["speaks", "is speak", "is spoken", "spoken"], answer: 2, solution: "Langkah 1: subjek English dikenai perbuatan, jadi kalimatnya pasif. Langkah 2: kalimatnya present tense, pola pasifnya is/am/are + verb-3. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah is spoken." },
    { q: "The homework must ___ before Friday.", options: ["submitted", "be submit", "submits", "be submitted"], answer: 3, solution: "Langkah 1: pola modal + be + verb-3 dipakai untuk kalimat pasif dengan modal. Langkah 2: must adalah modal dan submit adalah verb-1. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah be submitted." },
    { q: "If I were rich, I ___ travel around the world.", options: ["would", "will", "shall", "can"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: pola If + were menunjukkan conditional sentence type 2 (khayalan masa kini). Langkah 2: pada type 2, induk kalimat memakai would + verb-1. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah would." },
    { q: "If she had studied harder, she ___ passed the exam.", options: ["will have", "would have", "would", "had"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: pola If + had + verb-3 menunjukkan conditional sentence type 3 (penyesalan tentang masa lampau). Langkah 2: pada type 3, induk kalimat memakai would have + verb-3. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah would have." },
    { q: "I suggest that he ___ harder for the final test.", options: ["studies", "studied", "studying", "study"], answer: 3, solution: "Langkah 1: kata suggest yang diikuti that-clause memakai bentuk subjunctive. Langkah 2: dalam subjunctive, verb dipakai dalam bentuk dasar (bare infinitive) tanpa tambahan s/es. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah study." },
    { q: "I wish I ___ taller so I could join the basketball team.", options: ["were", "am", "will be", "be"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: wish + past tense dipakai untuk mengungkapkan khayalan yang berlawanan dengan kenyataan sekarang. Langkah 2: dalam pola ini, be selalu menjadi were untuk semua subjek. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah were." },
    { q: "Read the text: In a field, an ant worked hard all summer collecting food while the grasshopper sang and played. When winter came, the ant had plenty to eat, but the grasshopper went hungry. What is the moral of the story?", options: ["Laziness is acceptable", "Farmers are always poor", "Hard work leads to success", "Playing is more fun than working"], answer: 2, solution: "Langkah 1: perhatikan nasib kedua tokoh, semut yang rajin berkecukupan sedangkan belalang yang malas kelaparan. Langkah 2: perbedaan nasib itu disebabkan oleh kerja keras. Langkah 3: jadi pesan moralnya adalah kerja keras membawa keberhasilan." },
    { q: "Read the text: Single-use plastics pollute our oceans and kill marine life. Therefore, the government should ban them to protect the environment. What is the writer's position?", options: ["The writer opposes the ban on plastics", "The writer is neutral about plastics", "The writer supports producing more plastics", "The writer supports banning single-use plastics"], answer: 3, solution: "Langkah 1: temukan kata kunci pendirian penulis, yaitu should ban them. Langkah 2: kata should menunjukkan dukungan terhadap larangan. Langkah 3: jadi penulis mendukung pelarangan plastik sekali pakai." },
    { q: "The antonym of 'ancient' is ...", options: ["modern", "old", "antique", "classic"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: ancient artinya kuno atau berasal dari masa lampau. Langkah 2: antonim adalah lawan kata, jadi cari kata yang berarti baru atau masa kini. Langkah 3: modern adalah lawan kata yang tepat." },
    { q: "The word 'rapid' is closest in meaning to ...", options: ["slow", "fast", "calm", "late"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: rapid artinya cepat. Langkah 2: cari kata yang maknanya paling dekat. Langkah 3: fast berarti cepat, sehingga menjadi sinonim yang tepat." },
    { q: "Narrative texts mostly use ... to tell past events.", options: ["simple present tense", "present continuous tense", "future tense", "simple past tense"], answer: 3, solution: "Langkah 1: teks naratif menceritakan kejadian yang sudah berlalu. Langkah 2: tense yang dipakai untuk kejadian lampau adalah simple past tense. Langkah 3: jadi jawabannya simple past tense." },
    { q: "The bridge ___ in 1900.", options: ["was built", "built", "is built", "has built"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: jembatan dikenai perbuatan dibangun, jadi kalimatnya pasif. Langkah 2: tahun 1900 menunjukkan waktu lampau, pola pasifnya was/were + verb-3. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah was built." },
    { q: "If you heat ice, it ___.", options: ["will melt", "would melt", "melts", "melted"], answer: 2, solution: "Langkah 1: pola If + present tense dengan hasil yang selalu benar menunjukkan zero conditional (fakta umum). Langkah 2: pada zero conditional, induk kalimat juga memakai present tense. Langkah 3: jadi bentuk yang tepat adalah melts." },
    { q: "The synonym of 'enormous' is ...", options: ["tiny", "normal", "flat", "huge"], answer: 3, solution: "Langkah 1: enormous artinya sangat besar. Langkah 2: cari kata yang maknanya paling dekat. Langkah 3: huge berarti sangat besar, sehingga menjadi sinonim yang tepat." },
    { q: "The sentence 'The government should provide more green parks' is typical of a ... text.", options: ["narrative", "recount", "hortatory exposition", "descriptive"], answer: 2, solution: "Langkah 1: perhatikan kata should yang memberi saran atau anjuran. Langkah 2: teks yang bertujuan membujuk pembaca melakukan sesuatu dan memakai modal seperti should adalah hortatory exposition. Langkah 3: jadi jawabannya hortatory exposition." },
    { q: "In an analytical exposition text, the word 'therefore' signals that the next statement is a ...", options: ["contrast", "new example", "result or conclusion", "personal story"], answer: 2, solution: "Langkah 1: therefore adalah kata penghubung penanda akibat atau simpulan. Langkah 2: kata ini dipakai sebelum penulis menarik kesimpulan dari argumen-argumennya. Langkah 3: jadi pernyataan berikutnya adalah hasil atau simpulan." },
    { q: "Read the text: Long ago in a small village near Mount Bromo, there lived a kind old woman. Every morning she shared her food with hungry travelers. Where did the story take place?", options: ["In a big city", "In a small village near Mount Bromo", "On a ship", "In a forest"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: cari informasi latar tempat di bagian orientation teks. Langkah 2: kalimat pertama menyebut 'in a small village near Mount Bromo'. Langkah 3: jadi cerita berlatar di sebuah desa kecil dekat Gunung Bromo." },
    { q: "The generic structure of a hortatory exposition text is ...", options: ["orientation - complication - resolution", "thesis - arguments - recommendation", "identification - description", "newsworthy event - background events - source"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: hortatory exposition bertujuan membujuk pembaca melakukan sesuatu. Langkah 2: strukturnya diawali thesis (pendirian), diikuti arguments (alasan), dan diakhiri recommendation (anjuran). Langkah 3: jadi strukturnya adalah thesis - arguments - recommendation." },
    { q: "The social function of a hortatory exposition text is to ...", options: ["retell past events", "persuade readers to do or not to do something", "describe a particular person", "entertain readers with a funny story"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: hortatory exposition bersifat anjuran. Langkah 2: teks ini memuat ajakan atau saran agar pembaca bertindak. Langkah 3: jadi fungsinya adalah membujuk pembaca untuk melakukan atau tidak melakukan sesuatu." },
    { q: "Which language feature is commonly used in a hortatory exposition text?", options: ["modal verbs such as should and must", "direct speech of a witness", "rhyme and rhythm", "dialogue between characters"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: hortatory exposition berisi anjuran kepada pembaca. Langkah 2: anjuran biasanya dinyatakan dengan modal seperti should, must, dan ought to. Langkah 3: jadi ciri kebahasaannya adalah penggunaan modal verbs seperti should dan must." },
    { q: "Read the sentence: 'Smoking in public places harms non-smokers, so the local government should create more smoke-free zones.' This sentence is an example of a ...", options: ["thesis", "complication", "orientation", "coda"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: kalimat ini menyatakan pendirian penulis tentang merokok di tempat umum. Langkah 2: pada hortatory exposition, pendirian atau gagasan pokok penulis di awal teks disebut thesis. Langkah 3: jadi kalimat tersebut contoh thesis." },
    { q: "A hortatory exposition text mainly uses ... tense.", options: ["simple past", "simple present", "past perfect", "future continuous"], answer: 1, solution: "Langkah 1: hortatory exposition menyampaikan anjuran yang berlaku umum dan bersifat kekinian. Langkah 2: pernyataan umum dan anjuran memakai simple present tense. Langkah 3: jadi teks ini terutama memakai simple present tense." },
    { q: "The generic structure of a discussion text is ...", options: ["issue - arguments for - arguments against - conclusion", "thesis - arguments - recommendation", "orientation - events - reorientation", "identification - description"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: discussion text membahas suatu isu dari dua sisi yang berbeda. Langkah 2: strukturnya diawali issue (permasalahan), lalu arguments for (pendukung), arguments against (penentang), dan diakhiri conclusion atau recommendation. Langkah 3: jadi strukturnya adalah issue - arguments for - arguments against - conclusion." },
    { q: "The purpose of a discussion text is to ...", options: ["present different opinions about an issue", "tell a funny personal experience", "describe how to operate a machine", "persuade readers to buy a product"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: discussion berasal dari kata discuss yang berarti membahas. Langkah 2: teks ini menyajikan pandangan yang mendukung dan yang menentang suatu isu secara berimbang. Langkah 3: jadi tujuannya menyajikan pendapat-pendapat yang berbeda tentang suatu isu." },
    { q: "Which connective is typically used to introduce an opposing argument in a discussion text?", options: ["on the other hand", "for example", "in conclusion", "first of all"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: discussion text memuat argumen yang mendukung dan yang menentang. Langkah 2: untuk beralih dari sisi pendukung ke sisi penentang dipakai kata penghubung penanda pertentangan. Langkah 3: on the other hand adalah penghubung yang tepat untuk memperkenalkan argumen yang berlawanan." },
    { q: "In a discussion text, 'arguments against' are the reasons that ...", options: ["disagree with or oppose the issue", "support the issue", "describe the background", "quote an expert"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: arguments against berarti argumen-argumen yang menentang. Langkah 2: argumen ini berisi alasan-alasan yang tidak setuju dengan isu yang dibahas. Langkah 3: jadi arguments against adalah alasan-alasan yang tidak setuju atau menentang isu tersebut." },
    { q: "The final part of a discussion text usually contains the writer's ...", options: ["personal conclusion or recommendation", "new argument against", "dialogue", "advertisement"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: setelah menyajikan dua sisi argumen, penulis menutup teks. Langkah 2: bagian penutup berisi simpulan pribadi penulis atau saran berdasarkan kedua sisi tersebut. Langkah 3: jadi bagian akhir biasanya memuat simpulan atau saran pribadi penulis." },
    { q: "The generic structure of a news item text is ...", options: ["newsworthy event - background events - source", "thesis - arguments - reiteration", "orientation - complication - resolution", "goal - materials - steps"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: news item adalah teks berita tentang kejadian yang layak diberitakan. Langkah 2: strukturnya diawali newsworthy event (kejadian utama), diikuti background events (latar kejadian), dan diakhiri source (narasumber). Langkah 3: jadi strukturnya adalah newsworthy event - background events - source." },
    { q: "The 'newsworthy event' part of a news item text answers the questions ...", options: ["who, what, when, and where", "how to cook and serve", "why the writer is sad", "what the moral is"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: newsworthy event adalah ringkasan kejadian utama di awal berita. Langkah 2: ringkasan berita yang baik menjawab 5W+1H, terutama who, what, when, dan where. Langkah 3: jadi bagian ini menjawab pertanyaan siapa, apa, kapan, dan di mana." },
    { q: "The 'source' in a news item text usually contains ...", options: ["statements or quotes from witnesses or officials", "the writer's personal opinion", "a funny anecdote", "step-by-step instructions"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: source adalah bagian akhir teks berita. Langkah 2: bagian ini memuat pernyataan atau kutipan dari saksi, korban, atau pejabat sebagai penguat kebenaran berita. Langkah 3: jadi source biasanya berisi pernyataan atau kutipan dari saksi atau pejabat." },
    { q: "News item texts mainly use ... because they report events that have happened.", options: ["simple past tense", "simple present tense", "future tense", "present perfect continuous"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: berita melaporkan kejadian yang sudah terjadi. Langkah 2: kejadian lampau dalam bahasa Inggris dinyatakan dengan simple past tense. Langkah 3: jadi teks news item terutama memakai simple past tense." },
    { q: "Read the text: 'A 5.2-magnitude earthquake shook Cianjur last night. Dozens of houses were damaged, but no casualties were reported, according to the local disaster agency.' This text is a ...", options: ["news item", "narrative", "procedure", "descriptive"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: teks melaporkan kejadian gempa yang baru terjadi beserta dampaknya. Langkah 2: teks yang menginformasikan kejadian aktual yang layak diberitakan disebut news item. Langkah 3: jadi teks tersebut adalah news item." },
    { q: "Read the lyric: 'You raise me up, so I can stand on mountains.' The word 'mountains' in this lyric most likely symbolizes ...", options: ["great challenges or difficulties", "real mountains to climb", "a holiday destination", "geography lessons"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: lirik lagu sering memakai bahasa kiasan, bukan makna harfiah. Langkah 2: berdiri di atas gunung menggambarkan pencapaian tertinggi setelah melewati hal yang sulit. Langkah 3: jadi kata mountains melambangkan tantangan atau kesulitan besar." },
    { q: "A song lyric that tells about never giving up and fighting for dreams has the theme of ...", options: ["struggle and hope", "cooking food", "playing games", "shopping"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: tema adalah gagasan pokok sebuah lagu. Langkah 2: lirik tentang pantang menyerah dan berjuang meraih mimpi berbicara tentang perjuangan dan harapan. Langkah 3: jadi temanya adalah perjuangan dan harapan (struggle and hope)." },
    { q: "Read the lyric: 'Count your blessings, name them one by one.' The message of this lyric is ...", options: ["we should be grateful for what we have", "we must learn mathematics", "we should count money carefully", "we must buy many things"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: blessings berarti nikmat atau karunia. Langkah 2: ajakan untuk menghitung nikmat satu per satu bermakna mengingatkan kita untuk bersyukur. Langkah 3: jadi pesannya adalah kita harus bersyukur atas apa yang kita miliki." },
    { q: "Repetition of a line or phrase in song lyrics is usually used to ...", options: ["emphasize the main message of the song", "make the song longer only", "confuse the listeners", "fill the silence"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: pengulangan adalah teknik umum dalam lirik lagu, misalnya pada bagian reff. Langkah 2: bagian yang diulang biasanya memuat pesan terpenting yang ingin diingat pendengar. Langkah 3: jadi pengulangan dipakai untuk menekankan pesan utama lagu." },
    { q: "Read the lyric: 'Hello darkness, my old friend.' The mood created by this lyric is ...", options: ["gloomy and lonely", "cheerful and lively", "angry and violent", "funny and playful"], answer: 0, solution: "Langkah 1: perhatikan kata darkness (kegelapan) yang disapa sebagai kawan lama. Langkah 2: kegelapan dan kesendirian menciptakan suasana yang muram. Langkah 3: jadi suasana (mood) lirik tersebut adalah muram dan kesepian." },
{ q: "She _____ in this company since 2019, so she knows all the clients well.", options: ["is working", "worked", "has been working", "has worked"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Kata 'since 2019' menunjukkan aksi yang dimulai di masa lalu dan masih berlangsung sampai sekarang. 2. Untuk menekankan durasi aksi yang masih berjalan, dipakai Present Perfect Continuous: has/have + been + V-ing. 3. 'Has worked' memang mungkin, tetapi konteks 'sejak 2019 sampai sekarang' menuntut bentuk continuous. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'has been working'." },
{ q: "I can't open the door. I _____ my keys somewhere in the market.", options: ["lost", "lose", "have been losing", "have lost"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Kehilangan kunci adalah kejadian tunggal di masa lalu yang akibatnya masih terasa sekarang (pintu tidak bisa dibuka) → Present Perfect. 2. 'Lose' termasuk stative verb, sehingga tidak dipakai dalam bentuk continuous untuk makna 'kehilangan'. 3. 'Lost' (simple past) kurang tepat karena fokus kalimat adalah akibat di masa kini. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'have lost'." },
{ q: "When the guests arrived at 7 p.m., we _____ the food for two hours already.", options: ["have been preparing", "had been preparing", "prepared", "are preparing"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Ada dua kejadian lampau: tamu tiba (past simple) dan menyiapkan makanan yang terjadi lebih dulu. 2. Aksi yang lebih dulu plus durasi 'for two hours' memakai Past Perfect Continuous: had + been + V-ing. 3. 'Have been preparing' salah karena acuannya masa kini, bukan masa lampau. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had been preparing'." },
{ q: "By next June, Rania _____ her thesis and graduated.", options: ["will have finished", "will finish", "finishes", "would have finished"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Frasa 'by next June' menandakan aksi yang akan sudah selesai pada titik waktu di masa depan. 2. Polanya Future Perfect: will + have + V3. 3. 'Will finish' hanya menyatakan aksi masa depan tanpa makna 'sudah selesai'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'will have finished'." },
{ q: "Budi looks exhausted because he _____ football since 3 p.m.", options: ["has played", "played", "has been playing", "plays"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Kata 'since 3 p.m.' menunjukkan aksi dimulai di masa lalu dan masih relevan sekarang. 2. Kondisi Budi yang kelelahan menekankan durasi/aktivitas yang berlangsung → Present Perfect Continuous. 3. 'Has played' menekankan hasil, bukan aktivitas yang sedang berjalan. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'has been playing'." },
{ q: "Hurry up! The bus has just _____; we can still see its lights.", options: ["been leaving", "left", "leaves", "leave"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Kata 'just' (baru saja) dalam Present Perfect diikuti past participle (V3). 2. V3 dari 'leave' adalah 'left'. 3. 'Been leaving' salah karena 'leave' di sini adalah kejadian tunggal, bukan aktivitas berdurasi. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'left'." },
{ q: "We had already _____ dinner when our neighbor knocked on the door.", options: ["ate", "been eating", "eat", "eaten"], answer: 3, solution: "1. 'Had' menandakan Past Perfect, yang membutuhkan past participle (V3). 2. V3 dari 'eat' adalah 'eaten'. 3. 'Ate' adalah V2 (simple past), tidak bisa mengikuti 'had'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'eaten'." },
{ q: "By 8 a.m. tomorrow, the team _____ for twelve hours without a break.", options: ["will have been working", "will have worked", "will work", "would have been working"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Frasa 'by 8 a.m. tomorrow' + durasi 'for twelve hours' menuntut Future Perfect Continuous. 2. Polanya: will + have + been + V-ing. 3. 'Will have worked' menekankan penyelesaian, bukan durasi yang berlangsung. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'will have been working'." },
{ q: "She has known Dimas _____ they were classmates in junior high school.", options: ["for", "since", "during", "while"], answer: 1, solution: "1. 'They were classmates' adalah titik awal waktu (point in time), bukan durasi. 2. 'Since' dipakai untuk titik awal waktu, sedangkan 'for' untuk durasi. 3. 'During' dan 'while' tidak cocok dengan pola Present Perfect ini. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'since'." },
{ q: "I have _____ finished my assignment, so we can go out tonight.", options: ["yet", "still", "ever", "already"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Kalimat positif dengan makna 'sudah' memakai 'already', biasanya di antara have dan V3. 2. 'Yet' dipakai untuk kalimat negatif atau pertanyaan. 3. 'Still' dan 'ever' tidak cocok dengan makna kalimat ini. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'already'." },
{ q: "\"Have you heard from Sinta _____?\" \"No, she never replies.\"", options: ["lately", "just", "already", "since"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Pertanyaan menanyakan kabar 'akhir-akhir ini' → kata yang tepat adalah 'lately'. 2. 'Just' dan 'already' bermakna 'baru saja/sudah', tidak cocok untuk menanyakan kabar umum. 3. 'Since' butuh titik waktu setelahnya (since Monday). 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'lately'." },
{ q: "The movie _____ when the electricity suddenly went out.", options: ["has just started", "just started", "had just started", "just starts"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Ada dua kejadian lampau: film mulai (lebih dulu) dan listrik padam (kemudian). 2. Kejadian yang lebih dulu memakai Past Perfect: had + V3. 3. 'Has just started' salah karena acuannya masa lampau, bukan masa kini. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had just started'." },
{ q: "He _____ English for five years, but he still can't understand native speakers.", options: ["has learned", "has been learning", "learned", "learns"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Durasi 'for five years' yang masih berlangsung sampai sekarang menuntut Present Perfect Continuous. 2. Konteks 'masih belum bisa' menekankan proses belajar yang sedang berjalan. 3. 'Learned' (simple past) memutus hubungan dengan masa kini. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'has been learning'." },
{ q: "I _____ this old laptop for three years and it still works fine.", options: ["have", "have been having", "am having", "had"], answer: 0, solution: "1. 'Have' dalam arti 'memiliki' adalah stative verb, tidak dipakai dalam bentuk continuous. 2. 'Have been having' dan 'am having' salah untuk makna kepemilikan. 3. 'Had' (simple past) tidak cocok karena kepemilikan masih berlangsung. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'have'." },
{ q: "When I woke up this morning, my mother _____ breakfast for the whole family.", options: ["had already cooked", "has already cooked", "already cooks", "cooks already"], answer: 0, solution: "1. 'Woke up' adalah simple past; memasak terjadi sebelum itu → Past Perfect. 2. 'Already' diletakkan di antara had dan V3: had already cooked. 3. 'Has already cooked' salah karena acuannya masa lampau. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had already cooked'." },
{ q: "By the end of this year, Mr. Hendra _____ at this school for twenty years.", options: ["will have taught", "will teach", "will have been teaching", "would have taught"], answer: 2, solution: "1. 'By the end of this year' + durasi 'for twenty years' menuntut Future Perfect Continuous. 2. Polanya: will + have + been + V-ing. 3. 'Will have taught' menekankan penyelesaian, bukan durasi mengajar yang berlangsung. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'will have been teaching'." },
{ q: "We _____ anything about the exam schedule, so let's not spread rumors.", options: ["didn't hear nothing", "have not heard nothing", "don't hear", "haven't heard"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Kalimat negatif bahasa Inggris hanya memakai satu kata negatif; 'didn't hear nothing' adalah double negative yang salah. 2. Konteks 'sampai sekarang belum dengar' memakai Present Perfect negatif. 3. 'Don't hear' (simple present) tidak cocok untuk makna 'belum sampai sekarang'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'haven't heard'." },
{ q: "The baby _____ nonstop since midnight; the parents look exhausted.", options: ["has cried", "has been crying", "cried", "cries"], answer: 1, solution: "1. 'Since midnight' menunjukkan aksi dimulai di masa lalu dan masih relevan sekarang. 2. Menangis 'nonstop' menekankan aktivitas berdurasi → Present Perfect Continuous. 3. 'Cried' (simple past) memutus hubungan dengan kondisi orang tua yang kelelahan sekarang. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'has been crying'." },
{ q: "They _____ each other for years before they finally met in person.", options: ["had known", "have known", "knew", "know"], answer: 0, solution: "1. 'Met' adalah simple past; saling kenal terjadi jauh sebelumnya → Past Perfect. 2. 'Know' adalah stative verb, jadi bentuk continuous tidak dipakai. 3. 'Have known' salah karena periode saling kenal berakhir di masa lampau. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had known'." },
{ q: "The train had already _____ before we reached the station.", options: ["leaves", "been leaving", "left", "leave"], answer: 2, solution: "1. 'Had' menuntut past participle (V3). 2. V3 dari 'leave' adalah 'left'. 3. 'Been leaving' tidak cocok karena keberangkatan kereta adalah kejadian tunggal. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'left'." },
{ q: "\"_____ you _____ your homework yet?\" \"Yes, I did it an hour ago.\"", options: ["Did/finish", "Have/finished", "Have/finish", "Do/finish"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Kata 'yet' dalam pertanyaan memakai Present Perfect: Have/Has + subjek + V3. 2. 'Did finish' (simple past) tidak berpasangan dengan 'yet'. 3. 'Have finish' salah karena setelah have harus V3, bukan V1. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'Have/finished'." },
{ q: "He _____ in Jakarta since 2015, but last month he moved to Bandung.", options: ["has been living", "lives", "lived", "had been living"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Periode tinggal di Jakarta sudah berakhir bulan lalu (moved), jadi acuannya masa lampau. 2. Aksi berdurasi yang selesai di masa lampau memakai Past Perfect Continuous. 3. 'Has been living' salah karena ia tidak lagi tinggal di Jakarta. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had been living'." },
{ q: "By this time next week, the students _____ their final exams.", options: ["will have completed", "will complete", "complete", "would complete"], answer: 0, solution: "1. 'By this time next week' menandakan aksi yang sudah selesai pada titik waktu di masa depan. 2. Polanya Future Perfect: will + have + V3. 3. 'Will complete' tidak mengandung makna 'sudah selesai'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'will have completed'." },
{ q: "I _____ to the new dentist three times this year, and my teeth feel much better.", options: ["have gone", "went", "have been", "go"], answer: 2, solution: "1. 'Have been to' berarti pergi dan sudah kembali; 'have gone to' berarti pergi dan masih di sana. 2. Konteks giginya sudah membaik menunjukkan ia sudah pulang dari dokter gigi. 3. 'Went' (simple past) tidak cocok dengan 'three times this year' yang masih berjalan. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'have been'." },
{ q: "She realized she _____ her wallet at home only after the taxi arrived.", options: ["has left", "had left", "leaves", "leave"], answer: 1, solution: "1. 'Realized' dan 'arrived' adalah simple past; meninggalkan dompet terjadi lebih dulu. 2. Kejadian yang paling dulu memakai Past Perfect: had + V3. 3. 'Has left' salah karena seluruh konteks berada di masa lampau. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had left'." },
{ q: "The new bridge over the river _____ by the mayor last month.", options: ["was inaugurated", "inaugurated", "has inaugurated", "is inaugurate"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Penanda waktu 'last month' menunjukkan Simple Past. 2. Subjek 'bridge' menerima aksi (diresmikan) → passive: was/were + V3. 3. 'Inaugurated' saja adalah bentuk aktif, tidak cocok untuk subjek benda. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'was inaugurated'." },
{ q: "English _____ as a second language in many Asian countries.", options: ["is speak", "speaks", "is speaking", "is spoken"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Ini fakta umum di masa kini → Simple Present. 2. Subjek 'English' menerima aksi (dituturkan) → passive: is + V3. 3. 'Is speak' salah karena setelah is harus V3, bukan V1; 'is speaking' bermakna aktif 'sedang berbicara'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'is spoken'." },
{ q: "The documents _____ yet; the courier is still on the way.", options: ["didn't deliver", "haven't been delivered", "haven't delivered", "aren't deliver"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Kata 'yet' dengan konteks masa kini menuntut Present Perfect. 2. Subjek 'documents' menerima aksi → passive: have/has + been + V3. 3. 'Haven't delivered' adalah bentuk aktif yang butuh objek. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'haven't been delivered'." },
{ q: "The ballroom must _____ before the wedding guests arrive tonight.", options: ["clean", "be cleaning", "cleaned", "be cleaned"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Setelah modal (must), passive memakai pola: modal + be + V3. 2. 'Cleaned' saja tanpa 'be' tidak membentuk passive setelah modal. 3. 'Be cleaning' adalah bentuk aktif continuous, salah untuk subjek 'ballroom'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'be cleaned'." },
{ q: "All assignments should _____ by Friday at the latest.", options: ["be submitted", "submit", "be submitting", "submitted"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Setelah modal 'should', passive memakai pola: should + be + V3. 2. V3 dari 'submit' adalah 'submitted'. 3. 'Submit' saja adalah bentuk aktif yang tidak cocok untuk subjek 'assignments'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'be submitted'." },
{ q: "\"The manager offered the staff a bonus.\" → \"The staff _____ a bonus by the manager.\"", options: ["offered", "were offer", "were offered", "was offered"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Kalimat asli memakai 'offered' (simple past) dengan dua objek: the staff dan a bonus. 2. Saat 'the staff' menjadi subjek passive, polanya: were + V3 karena subjek jamak. 3. 'Was offered' salah karena subjeknya jamak. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'were offered'." },
{ q: "She _____ her hair _____ at the new salon yesterday.", options: ["has/cut", "had/cut", "have/cut", "had/to cut"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Ini causative 'have': subjek menyuruh orang lain melakukan aksi. 2. Kejadian 'yesterday' → Simple Past: had + objek + V3. 3. 'To cut' salah karena causative have tidak memakai 'to' infinitive. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had/cut'." },
{ q: "Doni _____ his motorcycle _____ last weekend because the engine broke down.", options: ["had/repair", "got/repair", "has/repaired", "got/repaired"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Ini causative 'get': get + objek + V3. 2. Kejadian 'last weekend' → Simple Past: got + objek + V3. 3. 'Got/repair' salah karena setelah objek harus V3, bukan V1. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'got/repaired'." },
{ q: "The classroom needs _____ before the new semester starts.", options: ["to be painted", "to paint", "painting", "to be paint"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Pola 'need' + passive infinitive: need + to be + V3. 2. Subjek 'classroom' menerima aksi pengecatan. 3. 'To paint' adalah infinitive aktif yang butuh pelaku jelas. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'to be painted'." },
{ q: "Rina dislikes _____ about behind her back.", options: ["to be talked", "talking", "being talked", "to talk"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Setelah 'dislike' dipakai gerund, dan maknanya pasif (dibicarakan) → being + V3. 2. 'Talking' adalah gerund aktif, maknanya menjadi 'tidak suka membicarakan', berbeda arti. 3. 'To be talked' salah karena dislike tidak diikuti to-infinitive. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'being talked'." },
{ q: "\"People believe that the old man can predict the weather.\" → \"The old man _____ to be able to predict the weather.\"", options: ["is believe", "is believed", "believes", "was believed"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Ini passive dari reporting verb: subjek + is/are + V3 + to-infinitive. 2. Karena keyakinan masih berlaku sekarang, dipakai 'is believed'. 3. 'Is believe' salah karena setelah is harus V3. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'is believed'." },
{ q: "\"_____ that the lake is haunted by a giant snake.\"", options: ["They say", "It says", "People are said", "It is said"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Pola impersonal passive untuk reporting verb: It + is + V3 + that. 2. 'It is said that...' adalah bentuk baku untuk 'konon/katanya'. 3. 'It says' salah karena 'it' tidak bisa menjadi pelaku 'say'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'It is said'." },
{ q: "In \"The thief was arrested last night,\" the agent is omitted because _____.", options: ["the doer is unknown or unimportant", "the sentence is in the active voice", "the verb is intransitive", "passive voice never uses an agent"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Agen (pelaku) dalam passive boleh dihilangkan jika tidak diketahui atau tidak penting. 2. Di sini yang penting adalah pencurinya tertangkap, bukan siapa yang menangkap. 3. Passive tetap bisa memakai agen dengan 'by' bila perlu. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'the doer is unknown or unimportant'." },
{ q: "\"The storm damaged the roof.\" → \"The roof _____.\"", options: ["was damage", "was damaged", "damaged", "has damage"], answer: 1, solution: "1. 'Damaged' adalah simple past → passive-nya was/were + V3. 2. V3 dari 'damage' adalah 'damaged'. 3. 'Was damage' salah karena setelah was harus V3, bukan V1. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'was damaged'." },
{ q: "Smoking _____ in this hospital area.", options: ["prohibits", "prohibit", "is prohibited", "prohibited"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Ini larangan umum di masa kini → Simple Present passive. 2. Subjek 'smoking' (gerund, tunggal) → is + V3. 3. 'Prohibited' saja tanpa to be bukan kalimat lengkap. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'is prohibited'." },
{ q: "\"Someone has stolen my bicycle!\" → \"My bicycle _____!\"", options: ["has stolen", "has been steal", "is stolen", "has been stolen"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Kalimat asli memakai Present Perfect (has stolen). 2. Passive Present Perfect: has/have + been + V3. 3. 'Has been steal' salah karena setelah been harus V3. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'has been stolen'." },
{ q: "\"They were repairing the road when we passed by.\" → \"The road _____ when we passed by.\"", options: ["was being repaired", "was repaired", "is being repaired", "has been repaired"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Kalimat asli memakai Past Continuous (were repairing). 2. Passive Past Continuous: was/were + being + V3. 3. Subjek 'the road' tunggal → 'was being repaired'. 4. 'Was repaired' (simple past) menghilangkan makna 'sedang'. 5. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'was being repaired'." },
{ q: "\"The new hospital will open next year.\" → \"The new hospital _____ next year.\"", options: ["will open", "will be opened", "will be open", "is opened"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Kalimat asli memakai 'will' (future). 2. Passive future: will + be + V3. 3. 'Will be open' salah karena 'open' di sini kata sifat, bukan V3. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'will be opened'." },
{ q: "\"The children ate all the cake.\" → \"All the cake _____.\"", options: ["was ate", "were eaten", "was eaten", "ate"], answer: 2, solution: "1. 'Ate' adalah simple past → passive: was/were + V3. 2. Subjek 'all the cake' dianggap tunggal → 'was eaten'. 3. 'Was ate' salah karena setelah was harus V3, bukan V2. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'was eaten'." },
{ q: "\"The mechanic can fix the car today.\" → \"The car _____ today.\"", options: ["can fix", "can fixed", "is can fix", "can be fixed"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Setelah modal 'can', passive memakai pola: can + be + V3. 2. V3 dari 'fix' adalah 'fixed'. 3. 'Can fixed' salah karena setelah modal tidak bisa langsung V3 tanpa 'be'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'can be fixed'." },
{ q: "\"The company promoted Andi to manager last week.\" → \"Andi _____ to manager last week.\"", options: ["was promoted", "promoted", "has promoted", "is promoted"], answer: 0, solution: "1. 'Promoted' adalah simple past → passive: was/were + V3. 2. Subjek 'Andi' tunggal → 'was promoted'. 3. 'Has promoted' adalah bentuk aktif perfect yang butuh objek. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'was promoted'." },
{ q: "\"The security guard told the visitors to wait outside.\" → \"The visitors _____ to wait outside.\"", options: ["told", "were tell", "were told", "are told"], answer: 2, solution: "1. 'Told' adalah simple past → passive: were + V3 karena subjek jamak. 2. V3 dari 'tell' adalah 'told'. 3. 'Were tell' salah karena setelah were harus V3. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'were told'." },
{ q: "We _____ the office _____ bright green before the inspection.", options: ["have/repainted", "had/repainted", "had/repaint", "get/repaint"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Ini causative 'have': subjek menyuruh orang lain mengecat. 2. Kejadian sebelum inspeksi di masa lalu → Simple Past: had + objek + V3. 3. 'Had/repaint' salah karena setelah objek harus V3. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had/repainted'." },
{ q: "\"People think that the suspect has left the country.\" → \"The suspect _____ to have left the country.\"", options: ["thinks", "is think", "was believed", "is believed"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Ini passive dari reporting verb dengan perfect infinitive karena aksi 'leave' terjadi sebelum 'think'. 2. Polanya: is + V3 + to have + V3. 3. 'Was believed' salah karena keyakinan masih berlaku sekarang. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'is believed'." },
{ q: "\"The committee postponed the meeting until Monday.\" → \"The meeting _____ until Monday.\"", options: ["was postponed", "postponed", "has postponed", "is postpone"], answer: 0, solution: "1. 'Postponed' adalah simple past → passive: was/were + V3. 2. Subjek 'the meeting' tunggal → 'was postponed'. 3. 'Has postponed' adalah bentuk aktif yang butuh objek. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'was postponed'." },
{ q: "If you heat ice, it _____.", options: ["will melt", "would melt", "melts", "melted"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Ini kebenaran umum/fakta ilmiah → Conditional Type 0. 2. Pola Type 0: If + simple present, simple present. 3. Subjek 'it' tunggal → verb + s: 'melts'. 4. 'Will melt' adalah Type 1, tidak cocok untuk fakta umum. 5. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'melts'." },
{ q: "If it rains tomorrow, we _____ the football match.", options: ["will cancel", "cancel", "would cancel", "canceled"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Kondisi 'tomorrow' adalah kemungkinan nyata di masa depan → Conditional Type 1. 2. Pola Type 1: If + simple present, will + V1. 3. 'Would cancel' adalah Type 2 untuk pengandaian yang tidak nyata. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'will cancel'." },
{ q: "If I _____ rich, I would travel around the world.", options: ["am", "were", "will be", "had been"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Klausa utama memakai 'would' → Conditional Type 2 (pengandaian tidak nyata di masa kini). 2. Pola Type 2: If + simple past, would + V1. 3. Untuk 'be' dalam Type 2 selalu dipakai 'were' untuk semua subjek. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'were'." },
{ q: "If you had studied harder, you _____ the scholarship exam.", options: ["will pass", "would pass", "pass", "would have passed"], answer: 3, solution: "1. 'Had studied' adalah past perfect → Conditional Type 3 (penyesalan masa lalu). 2. Pola Type 3: If + past perfect, would + have + V3. 3. 'Would pass' adalah Type 2, tidak cocok dengan kondisi masa lalu. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'would have passed'." },
{ q: "If she had caught the earlier bus, she _____ here with us now.", options: ["would have been", "will be", "would be", "is"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Klausa if memakai past perfect (kondisi masa lalu), tetapi hasilnya 'now' (masa kini) → mixed conditional. 2. Pola mixed: If + past perfect, would + V1 (untuk hasil masa kini). 3. 'Would have been' salah karena hasilnya bukan di masa lalu. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'would be'." },
{ q: "If I were more confident, I _____ for that manager position last year.", options: ["would have applied", "will apply", "would apply", "apply"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Klausa if memakai simple past 'were' (kondisi kini), tetapi ada penanda 'last year' → mixed conditional. 2. Pola mixed: If + simple past, would + have + V3 (untuk hasil masa lalu). 3. 'Would apply' salah karena melamar terjadi tahun lalu. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'would have applied'." },
{ q: "_____ I known about the traffic jam, I would have left home earlier.", options: ["If", "Had", "Would", "Should"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Ini inverted conditional Type 3: 'had' dipindah ke depan menggantikan 'if'. 2. Bentuk lengkapnya: 'If I had known...' → 'Had I known...'. 3. 'Would' dan 'should' tidak bisa menggantikan 'if' di Type 3. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'Had'." },
{ q: "_____ I the principal, I would ban homework on weekends.", options: ["Was", "Am", "If", "Were"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Ini inverted conditional Type 2: 'were' dipindah ke depan menggantikan 'if'. 2. Bentuk lengkapnya: 'If I were the principal...' → 'Were I the principal...'. 3. 'Was' tidak dipakai dalam pengandaian Type 2. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'Were'." },
{ q: "_____ you need any help during the exam, please raise your hand.", options: ["Should", "Had", "Were", "If only"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Ini inverted conditional Type 1: 'should' dipindah ke depan menggantikan 'if'. 2. Bentuk lengkapnya: 'If you should need...' → 'Should you need...'. 3. Maknanya: 'seandainya kamu butuh bantuan'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'Should'." },
{ q: "I wish I _____ speak Japanese fluently like my sister.", options: ["can", "will", "could", "would"], answer: 2, solution: "1. 'Wish' untuk harapan yang tidak nyata di masa kini memakai bentuk lampau. 2. 'Can' harus di-backshift menjadi 'could'. 3. 'Will' tidak mengalami backshift yang benar di sini. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'could'." },
{ q: "I wish I _____ the last train last night; I had to sleep at the station.", options: ["didn't miss", "hadn't missed", "don't miss", "haven't missed"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Penyesalan tentang masa lalu ('last night') memakai wish + past perfect. 2. Polanya: wish + had + V3 (negatif: hadn't + V3). 3. 'Didn't miss' adalah simple past, hanya untuk harapan masa kini. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'hadn't missed'." },
{ q: "If only I _____ more time to finish this project!", options: ["have", "will have", "had had", "had"], answer: 3, solution: "1. 'If only' untuk harapan masa kini memakai bentuk lampau seperti Type 2. 2. 'Have' harus di-backshift menjadi 'had'. 3. 'Had had' berlebihan karena hanya satu kata kerja 'have' yang perlu diubah. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had'." },
{ q: "He talks as if he _____ everything about politics.", options: ["knows", "had known", "knew", "know"], answer: 2, solution: "1. 'As if' untuk pengandaian yang tidak nyata memakai subjunctive bentuk lampau. 2. Untuk masa kini yang tidak nyata: as if + simple past. 3. 'Knows' (present) salah karena faktanya ia tidak tahu segalanya. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'knew'." },
{ q: "She spends money as though she _____ a millionaire.", options: ["were", "is", "was be", "are"], answer: 0, solution: "1. 'As though' untuk pengandaian tidak nyata memakai subjunctive. 2. Untuk kata kerja 'be', subjunctive memakai 'were' untuk semua subjek. 3. 'Is' salah karena faktanya ia bukan jutawan. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'were'." },
{ q: "You won't pass the driving test _____ you practice seriously.", options: ["if", "unless", "when", "while"], answer: 1, solution: "1. 'Unless' berarti 'kecuali jika' = 'if...not'. 2. Kalimat ini bermakna 'kamu tidak akan lulus kecuali kamu berlatih serius'. 3. 'If' tanpa 'not' akan membalik makna kalimat. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'unless'." },
{ q: "You can borrow my laptop _____ you return it tonight.", options: ["unless", "if only", "as if", "provided that"], answer: 3, solution: "1. 'Provided that' berarti 'asalkan/dengan syarat', cocok untuk syarat meminjam. 2. 'Unless' berarti 'kecuali jika', maknanya berlawanan dengan maksud kalimat. 3. 'As if' untuk pengandaian, tidak cocok di sini. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'provided that'." },
{ q: "If you see Bagas at school, _____ him to return my book.", options: ["tell", "will tell", "would tell", "told"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Conditional Type 1 bisa diikuti imperative (perintah) di klausa utama. 2. Polanya: If + simple present, V1 (imperative). 3. 'Will tell' tidak dipakai untuk perintah langsung. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'tell'." },
{ q: "If he _____ to resign suddenly, the whole project would collapse.", options: ["will", "is", "were", "would"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Klausa utama memakai 'would' → Conditional Type 2. 2. Pola khusus 'were to + V1' dipakai untuk kemungkinan kecil di masa depan. 3. 'Will' dan 'would' tidak bisa muncul di klausa if. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'were'." },
{ q: "_____ you hurry, you will miss the last bus home.", options: ["If", "Unless", "When", "While"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Makna kalimat: 'kecuali kamu bergegas, kamu akan ketinggalan bus'. 2. 'Unless' = 'if...not', tepat untuk makna ini. 3. 'If you hurry' justru bermakna sebaliknya (akan dapat bus). 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'Unless'." },
{ q: "If it should rain during the ceremony, we _____ move indoors.", options: ["will", "would", "will have", "would have"], answer: 0, solution: "1. 'If + should' adalah Conditional Type 1 untuk kemungkinan kecil di masa depan. 2. Pola Type 1: If + simple present, will + V1. 3. 'Would' adalah Type 2, tidak cocok dengan 'should' di klausa if. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'will'." },
{ q: "\"I am very tired,\" she said. → She said that she _____ very tired.", options: ["is", "was", "has been", "will be"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Reported speech memakai backshift: simple present → simple past. 2. 'Am' berubah menjadi 'was' mengikuti subjek 'she'. 3. 'Is' dan 'has been' tidak mengalami backshift. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'was'." },
{ q: "\"I have finished my homework,\" he said. → He said that he _____ his homework.", options: ["has finished", "finishes", "will finish", "had finished"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Backshift: present perfect → past perfect. 2. 'Have finished' berubah menjadi 'had finished'. 3. 'Has finished' tidak mengalami backshift sehingga salah. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had finished'." },
{ q: "\"Are you coming to my party?\" she asked me. → She asked me _____ coming to her party.", options: ["if I was", "that I was", "I was", "whether was I"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Pertanyaan yes-no dalam reported speech memakai 'if' atau 'whether'. 2. Urutan kata kembali normal (subjek + verb), bukan inversi: 'if I was'. 3. 'Whether was I' salah karena masih memakai urutan tanya. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'if I was'." },
{ q: "\"Where do you live?\" he asked me. → He asked me where _____.", options: ["do I live", "did I live", "I lived", "I live"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Pertanyaan wh- memakai kata tanya yang sama: 'where'. 2. Urutan kata kembali normal dan tense di-backshift: 'do you live' → 'I lived'. 3. 'Do I live' salah karena masih memakai urutan tanya. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'I lived'." },
{ q: "\"Close the window, please,\" the teacher said. → The teacher _____ us to close the window.", options: ["said", "told", "asked to", "says"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Perintah dalam reported speech memakai pola: told/asked + objek + to-infinitive. 2. 'Said' tidak bisa diikuti objek + to-infinitive. 3. 'Says' salah karena reporting verb harus lampau. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'told'." },
{ q: "\"Please lend me your pen,\" Rani said to me. → Rani _____ me to lend her my pen.", options: ["told", "said", "ordered", "asked"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Kata 'please' menunjukkan permintaan (request), bukan perintah keras. 2. Reporting verb yang tepat untuk permintaan adalah 'asked'. 3. 'Ordered' terlalu keras untuk konteks meminjam pulpen. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'asked'." },
{ q: "\"You should see a doctor,\" he said. → He _____ me to see a doctor.", options: ["advised", "said", "told that", "suggested to"], answer: 0, solution: "1. 'Should' dalam saran dilaporkan dengan reporting verb 'advise'. 2. Polanya: advised + objek + to-infinitive. 3. 'Suggested to' salah karena suggest tidak diikuti to-infinitive. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'advised'." },
{ q: "\"Don't touch the electric wire!\" he said. → He _____ me not to touch the electric wire.", options: ["said", "told to", "warned", "warned to"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Larangan tentang bahaya dilaporkan dengan 'warn'. 2. Polanya: warned + objek + not + to-infinitive (tanpa 'to' setelah warned). 3. 'Warned to' salah karena warn tidak diikuti 'to' sebelum objek. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'warned'." },
{ q: "\"Let's go to the beach this weekend,\" she said. → She suggested _____ to the beach that weekend.", options: ["to go", "going", "go", "to going"], answer: 1, solution: "1. 'Suggest' diikuti gerund, bukan to-infinitive. 2. 'Let's go' dilaporkan menjadi 'suggested going'. 3. 'To go' salah karena suggest tidak memakai to-infinitive. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'going'." },
{ q: "\"I will call you tomorrow,\" he said. → He said he would call me _____.", options: ["the next day", "tomorrow", "yesterday", "the day"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Backshift: will → would. 2. Keterangan waktu ikut berubah: tomorrow → the next day. 3. 'Tomorrow' tidak boleh dipertahankan dalam reported speech. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'the next day'." },
{ q: "\"I left my bag here,\" she said. → She said she had left her bag _____.", options: ["here", "this", "now", "there"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Backshift: simple past 'left' → past perfect 'had left'. 2. Keterangan tempat ikut berubah: here → there. 3. 'Here' tidak boleh dipertahankan karena sudut pandang sudah berpindah. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'there'." },
{ q: "She _____ me that she couldn't come to the meeting.", options: ["said", "asked", "told", "suggested"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Pola 'tell' memakai objek: told + me + that. 2. 'Said' tidak bisa diikuti objek langsung ('said me' salah). 3. 'Asked' dan 'suggested' tidak cocok untuk menyampaikan pernyataan. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'told'." },
{ q: "\"I can swim across the river,\" he said. → He said he _____ swim across the river.", options: ["can", "could", "will", "may"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Backshift modal: can → could. 2. Modal 'can' tidak boleh dipertahankan dalam reported speech. 3. 'Will' dan 'may' mengubah makna kalimat asli. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'could'." },
{ q: "\"Do you like spicy food?\" she asked. → She asked me _____ spicy food.", options: ["if I liked", "that I like", "did I like", "whether do I like"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Pertanyaan yes-no memakai 'if'/'whether' + klausa normal. 2. Backshift: simple present 'do you like' → simple past 'I liked'. 3. 'Did I like' salah karena masih memakai urutan tanya. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'if I liked'." },
{ q: "\"Don't be late for school!\" mother said. → Mother _____ me not to be late for school.", options: ["said", "asked", "told", "says"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Perintah negatif dilaporkan dengan: told + objek + not + to-infinitive. 2. 'Said' tidak bisa diikuti objek + to-infinitive. 3. 'Says' salah karena reporting verb harus bentuk lampau. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'told'." },
{ q: "\"I must leave now,\" he said. → He said he _____ leave then.", options: ["must", "has to", "will", "had to"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Backshift: must → had to. 2. Keterangan waktu ikut berubah: now → then. 3. 'Must' umumnya tidak dipertahankan dalam reported speech. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had to'." },
{ q: "\"We are moving to Jakarta next week,\" they said. → They said they were moving to Jakarta _____.", options: ["the following week", "next week", "last week", "this week"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Backshift: present continuous 'are moving' → past continuous 'were moving'. 2. Keterangan waktu ikut berubah: next week → the following week. 3. 'Next week' tidak boleh dipertahankan dalam reported speech. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'the following week'." },
{ q: "\"Did you watch the match last night?\" he asked me. → He asked me if I _____ the match the night before.", options: ["watch", "had watched", "have watched", "watched"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Backshift: simple past 'did you watch' → past perfect 'had watched'. 2. Keterangan waktu ikut berubah: last night → the night before. 3. Urutan kata kembali normal setelah 'if'. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'had watched'." },
{ q: "\"What time does the train leave?\" she asked. → She asked what time the train _____.", options: ["does leave", "did leave", "left", "leaves"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Pertanyaan wh- memakai kata tanya yang sama dan urutan kata normal. 2. Backshift: simple present 'does leave' → simple past 'left'. 3. 'Does leave' salah karena masih memakai urutan tanya. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'left'." },
{ q: "\"Be quiet!\" the librarian said. → The librarian _____ them to be quiet.", options: ["told", "said", "asked that", "says"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Perintah dilaporkan dengan: told + objek + to-infinitive. 2. 'Said' tidak bisa diikuti objek + to-infinitive. 3. 'Asked that' bukan pola yang benar untuk perintah. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'told'." },
{ q: "\"I'll help you with your homework,\" he said. → He _____ to help me with my homework.", options: ["said", "told", "asked", "promised"], answer: 3, solution: "1. 'I'll help you' adalah janji (promise), bukan sekadar pernyataan. 2. Reporting verb yang tepat untuk janji adalah 'promised'. 3. Polanya: promised + to-infinitive. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'promised'." },
{ q: "\"I'm sorry I'm late,\" she said. → She apologized _____ late.", options: ["to be", "for being", "that late", "being"], answer: 1, solution: "1. 'Apologize' diikuti pola: apologized + for + gerund. 2. 'I'm sorry I'm late' menjadi 'apologized for being late'. 3. 'To be' salah karena apologize tidak memakai to-infinitive. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'for being'." },
{ q: "\"Water boils at 100°C,\" the teacher said. → The teacher said that water _____ at 100°C.", options: ["boils", "boiled", "will boil", "had boiled"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Fakta umum/kebenaran universal tidak mengalami backshift dalam reported speech. 2. Tense tetap simple present: 'boils'. 3. 'Boiled' salah karena fakta ilmiah tidak berubah. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'boils'." },
{ q: "\"This is the best restaurant in town,\" he said. → He said that _____ was the best restaurant in town.", options: ["this", "these", "that", "those"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Kata penunjuk ikut berubah dalam reported speech: this → that. 2. Subjeknya tunggal ('is'), jadi yang tepat 'that'. 3. 'Those' salah karena subjeknya tunggal. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'that'." },
{ q: "\"Open your books to page ten,\" the teacher said. → The teacher _____ the students to open their books to page ten.", options: ["said", "told that", "asked that", "asked"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Ini instruksi/perintah yang disampaikan dengan nada meminta → 'asked'. 2. Polanya: asked + objek + to-infinitive. 3. 'Told that' dan 'asked that' bukan pola yang benar. 4. Jadi jawaban yang tepat adalah 'asked'." }
,
{ q: "Read the text. \"Long ago, in a small fishing village, there lived a kind old man named Pak Darma. Every morning he sailed his tiny boat into the wide sea. One stormy night, a strange light appeared above the waves.\" Which part of the generic structure is shown?", options: ["Complication", "Coda", "Orientation", "Resolution"], answer: 2, solution: "1. The passage introduces the setting (a fishing village, long ago), the character (Pak Darma), and the background situation. 2. Introducing who, when, and where is the job of the orientation. 3. No problem has appeared yet, so it cannot be the complication or resolution." },
{ q: "\"Sinta climbed the hill to pick rare flowers. Suddenly, the ground beneath her cracked and she slid into a deep hole. She screamed, but nobody heard her.\" Which sentence shows the complication?", options: ["Sinta climbed the hill to pick rare flowers.", "She screamed, but nobody heard her.", "The ground beneath her cracked and she slid into a deep hole.", "The hole was deep and dark."], answer: 2, solution: "1. The complication is the part where the problem or crisis begins. 2. The ground cracking and Sinta falling is the turning point that creates the problem. 3. The first sentence is orientation, while the scream is a reaction to the problem that has already started." },
{ q: "\"With the last of his strength, Bima pulled the rope and freed the trapped deer. The deer bowed its head in thanks and vanished into the forest. Bima walked home with a light heart.\" Which part of the generic structure is shown?", options: ["Orientation", "Complication", "Coda", "Resolution"], answer: 3, solution: "1. The problem (the trapped deer) is solved when Bima frees it. 2. The part where the crisis is resolved is called the resolution. 3. A coda would add a moral or closing comment, which is absent here." },
{ q: "\"From that day on, the villagers never wasted food again, for they had learned that greed brings nothing but hunger.\" The sentence above functions as a ...", options: ["orientation", "coda", "complication", "resolution"], answer: 1, solution: "1. A coda is an optional closing part that gives a moral lesson or comment. 2. This sentence states the moral value the villagers learned. 3. Therefore it functions as the coda, not as part of the main plot." },
{ q: "\"Maya ran through the dark forest, climbed the old tower, and shouted for help.\" The verbs \"ran\", \"climbed\", and \"shouted\" show that narrative texts mainly use ...", options: ["the simple present tense", "the future tense", "the present continuous tense", "the simple past tense"], answer: 3, solution: "1. All three verbs are in past-tense form. 2. Narratives retell events that already happened, so they dominantly use the simple past tense. 3. Present and future tenses do not match the verb forms shown." },
{ q: "Which of the following is an action verb commonly found in narratives?", options: ["seized", "beautiful", "quickly", "happiness"], answer: 0, solution: "1. An action verb expresses something a character does. 2. \"Seized\" means grabbed - a physical action. 3. The others are an adjective, an adverb, and a noun, not action verbs." },
{ q: "\"First, the hunter set a trap near the river. Then, he hid behind the bushes. After a while, a mouse deer approached the trap.\" The words \"First\", \"Then\", and \"After a while\" are ...", options: ["action verbs", "time connectives", "descriptive adjectives", "direct speeches"], answer: 1, solution: "1. These words link events in the order they happened. 2. Words that sequence events in time are called time connectives. 3. They are not verbs, adjectives, or speech." },
{ q: "Read the fable. \"A proud eagle mocked a little sparrow for its plain feathers. One winter, the eagle's heavy wings froze in a storm, while the sparrow sheltered safely in a hollow tree. Ashamed, the eagle apologized and the two became friends.\" What is the moral value of the story?", options: ["Always migrate before winter arrives.", "Friendship can only happen between equals.", "Do not look down on others because of their appearance.", "Storms are dangerous for all birds."], answer: 2, solution: "1. The eagle's trouble comes from its pride and mockery of the sparrow. 2. The humble sparrow survives, and the eagle learns humility. 3. The lesson is about not judging or belittling others." },
{ q: "\"Where are you going?\" asked the old woman. \"To the market,\" replied the boy. The use of direct speech in a narrative mainly serves to ...", options: ["change the tense of the story", "replace the need for action verbs", "shorten the orientation", "make the characters feel alive and real"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Direct speech shows the characters' own words. 2. Hearing characters speak makes them vivid and realistic for readers. 3. It does not change tense or replace other language features." },
{ q: "\"They say the big banyan tree at the edge of the village grew from a walking stick planted by a holy man centuries ago.\" A story like this, explaining the origin of a place or thing, is called a ...", options: ["fable", "legend", "fairy tale", "myth"], answer: 1, solution: "1. This story explains how something in the real world came to be. 2. Traditional stories about the origins of places or things are called legends. 3. Fables teach morals through animals, and fairy tales center on magic." },
{ q: "Which element is typical of a fairy tale but NOT typical of a fable?", options: ["A magical spell that changes a person's form", "Animals that talk and behave like humans", "A clear moral lesson at the end", "A simple plot with few characters"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Talking animals and moral lessons appear in both fables and fairy tales. 2. Magic spells, witches, and enchantments are hallmarks of fairy tales. 3. Fables rarely rely on magic; they teach through animal behavior." },
{ q: "\"Although he was the youngest, Raka was the bravest of all the sailors.\" This sentence mainly shows ...", options: ["the complication", "the setting", "characterization", "a time connective"], answer: 2, solution: "1. The sentence describes Raka's personal quality (bravery). 2. Revealing what a character is like is called characterization. 3. It introduces no problem, place, or time sequence." },
{ q: "\"Dewi had to choose between saving her brother and saving the village's rice supply.\" The main conflict in this story is ...", options: ["a fight between two villages", "a natural disaster", "a misunderstanding between friends", "an internal conflict"], answer: 3, solution: "1. The struggle happens inside Dewi's mind - a difficult moral choice. 2. A conflict within a character's own thoughts or feelings is an internal conflict. 3. No second village, disaster, or quarreling friends are involved." },
{ q: "\"By the time the rescue team arrived, the old man had already left the cave.\" The verb form \"had left\" is used to show that ...", options: ["the leaving happens right now", "the leaving happened before the team's arrival", "the leaving will happen tomorrow", "the leaving happens regularly"], answer: 1, solution: "1. \"Had left\" is the past perfect tense. 2. The past perfect shows the earlier of two past events. 3. Here it marks that the man left before the rescue team arrived." },
{ q: "Arrange these events into the correct plot order: (1) The prince defeats the dragon. (2) A dragon burns the prince's village. (3) The prince trains with a wise hermit. (4) The village celebrates in peace.", options: ["2 - 3 - 1 - 4", "1 - 2 - 3 - 4", "2 - 1 - 3 - 4", "3 - 2 - 4 - 1"], answer: 0, solution: "1. A narrative follows: problem appears, struggle, climax, then resolution. 2. The dragon attack (2) starts the problem, training (3) is the struggle, the defeat (1) is the climax, and the celebration (4) closes the story. 3. Only 2-3-1-4 follows this logical sequence." },
{ q: "\"Dear Diary, Yesterday was unforgettable! My family and I hiked to the top of Mount Penanggungan. We started at dawn and reached the peak just as the sun rose.\" This text is a ...", options: ["factual recount", "personal recount", "narrative", "descriptive text"], answer: 1, solution: "1. The text retells the writer's own past experience in the first person. 2. A recount of personal experience is called a personal recount. 3. It is not fiction (narrative) nor an official report (factual recount)." },
{ q: "\"At 8:15 a.m., a bus skidded on the wet road near the market. Two passengers suffered minor injuries. Police arrived ten minutes later and cleared the scene.\" This text is a ...", options: ["personal recount", "legend", "factual recount", "procedure text"], answer: 2, solution: "1. The text reports an actual incident objectively, with exact time and facts. 2. An objective report of an event is a factual recount. 3. There is no \"I/we\" personal voice, so it is not personal." },
{ q: "\"We finally arrived home at midnight, tired but happy. It was truly a holiday to remember.\" In a recount text, these sentences function as the ...", options: ["orientation", "sequence of events", "title", "reorientation"], answer: 3, solution: "1. These closing sentences give a personal comment and wrap up the story. 2. The optional closing of a recount is called the reorientation. 3. The orientation opens the text, and the events form the middle." },
{ q: "Which group contains sequence words typically used in a recount?", options: ["first, then, after that, finally", "because, since, therefore, so", "however, although, whereas, but", "very, really, extremely, quite"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Recounts retell events in chronological order. 2. \"First, then, after that, finally\" mark the order of events. 3. The other groups show cause, contrast, or intensity - not sequence." },
{ q: "\"Last holiday, we ___ to the beach and ___ sandcastles all afternoon.\" The correct past-tense verbs are ...", options: ["go - build", "went - built", "went - build", "go - built"], answer: 1, solution: "1. \"Last holiday\" signals the simple past tense. 2. The past forms are \"went\" (go) and \"built\" (build). 3. Present forms do not fit a finished past event." },
{ q: "\"On Sunday morning, my classmates and I cleaned the school garden.\" In a recount, this sentence belongs to the ...", options: ["reorientation", "coda", "orientation", "recommendation"], answer: 2, solution: "1. It tells who (my classmates and I), when (Sunday morning), and where (school garden). 2. Introducing participants, time, and place is the orientation's job. 3. A recount has no coda or recommendation." },
{ q: "The main difference between a personal recount and a factual recount is ...", options: ["personal recounts are always fiction; factual recounts are always true", "personal recounts use present tense; factual recounts use past tense", "personal recounts have no structure; factual recounts have orientation", "personal recounts express the writer's feelings; factual recounts stay objective"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Both retell past events and share the same basic structure. 2. The difference lies in voice: personal recounts include feelings and \"I\", while factual recounts report objectively. 3. Both use past tense and both can have orientation, events, and reorientation." },
{ q: "Which text is a recount rather than a narrative?", options: ["\"Last month our school held a charity bazaar. We raised two million rupiah for flood victims.\"", "\"Once upon a time, a clever mouse deer tricked a hungry crocodile.\"", "\"The Borobudur Temple is the largest Buddhist temple in the world.\"", "\"First, boil the water. Then, add the noodles and stir.\""], answer: 0, solution: "1. A recount retells real past events without a fictional plot. 2. The bazaar text reports something that actually happened, in past tense. 3. The second is a fable (narrative), the third describes, and the fourth gives instructions." },
{ q: "\"I felt nervous when I stepped onto the stage, but the applause made me smile.\" The pronoun \"I\" and the feeling described show that the text is a ...", options: ["factual recount", "personal recount", "news item", "analytical exposition"], answer: 1, solution: "1. First-person pronouns and personal feelings mark the writer's own experience. 2. That is the hallmark of a personal recount. 3. Factual recounts and news items avoid personal feelings." },
{ q: "Put the recount events in order: (1) We packed our bags the night before. (2) We watched the sunrise from the campsite. (3) We arrived at the campsite at dusk. (4) We hiked down the mountain in the morning.", options: ["2 - 1 - 3 - 4", "1 - 2 - 3 - 4", "1 - 3 - 2 - 4", "3 - 1 - 4 - 2"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Recounts follow chronological order. 2. Packing (1) comes first, arrival at dusk (3) next, sunrise (2) the next morning, then hiking down (4). 3. Only 1-3-2-4 respects the time logic." },
{ q: "\"My cat, Miko, is a round, fluffy Persian with emerald-green eyes. He loves sleeping on the warm sofa and purrs loudly when I stroke his back.\" Which sentence is the identification?", options: ["The sofa in our living room is very comfortable.", "My cat, Miko, is a round, fluffy Persian with emerald-green eyes.", "He purrs loudly when I stroke his back.", "Warm sofas make cats sleepy in the afternoon."], answer: 1, solution: "1. Identification introduces the object being described. 2. The sentence naming Miko and stating what he is introduces him. 3. The other sentences describe habits or unrelated things." },
{ q: "\"The waterfall ___ crystal clear and ___ a soothing sound that calms every visitor.\" The correct present-tense verbs are ...", options: ["was - made", "are - make", "is - made", "is - makes"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Descriptive texts use the simple present tense for timeless facts. 2. \"Waterfall\" is singular, so it takes \"is\" and \"makes\". 3. Past forms would wrongly suggest the description is over." },
{ q: "Choose the sentence with the CORRECT adjective order.", options: ["She wore a red beautiful silk dress.", "She wore a beautiful red silk dress.", "She wore a silk beautiful red dress.", "She wore a beautiful silk red dress."], answer: 1, solution: "1. Adjective order runs: opinion, then color, then material. 2. \"Beautiful\" (opinion), \"red\" (color), \"silk\" (material) is the correct sequence. 3. The other options scramble this fixed order." },
{ q: "\"The bakery filled the street with the warm aroma of freshly baked bread.\" This sensory detail appeals to the sense of ...", options: ["smell", "sight", "hearing", "touch"], answer: 0, solution: "1. \"Aroma\" refers to a scent carried through the air. 2. Smell is the sense that detects aromas. 3. Sight, hearing, and touch are not triggered by an aroma." },
{ q: "In descriptive texts, verbs like \"is\", \"has\", and \"looks\" are called ...", options: ["action verbs", "modal verbs", "relating verbs", "phrasal verbs"], answer: 2, solution: "1. These verbs link the subject to its description rather than showing action. 2. Verbs that connect a subject to its characteristics are relating (linking) verbs. 3. They are not modals or phrasal verbs, and they show no action." },
{ q: "Which sentence describes a place most vividly?", options: ["The beach was crowded yesterday.", "We went to the beach by bus.", "The beach is 5 kilometers from here.", "The beach has white sand, gentle waves, and tall coconut trees."], answer: 3, solution: "1. Vivid description needs descriptive adjectives. 2. \"White\", \"gentle\", and \"tall\" paint a sensory picture of the beach. 3. The other options state facts or actions without describing." },
{ q: "\"An old, mysterious mansion stood at the end of the quiet street.\" The adjectives in the sentence are ...", options: ["stood, end, street", "an, the, at", "old, mysterious, quiet", "mansion, street, end"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Adjectives describe nouns. 2. \"Old\" and \"mysterious\" describe the mansion; \"quiet\" describes the street. 3. The other options list verbs, articles, nouns, or prepositions." },
{ q: "A descriptive text about a person mostly focuses on ...", options: ["physical appearance, character, and habits", "the steps to make something", "a sequence of past events", "arguments for and against an issue"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Describing a person means portraying what they are like. 2. Appearance, personality, and habits are the content of personal description. 3. Steps belong to procedures; events to recounts; arguments to discussions." },
{ q: "\"Komodo dragons ___ strong jaws and sharp claws. They ___ on deer and wild boar.\" The correct verbs are ...", options: ["has - feeds", "have - feed", "had - fed", "having - feeding"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Descriptive texts about animals in general use the simple present. 2. \"Dragons\" is plural, so the verbs are \"have\" and \"feed\". 3. Singular or past forms break subject-verb agreement or tense." },
{ q: "Which text is descriptive?", options: ["\"I woke up at five, took a shower, and rushed to school.\"", "\"The classroom should have better lighting because students need it.\"", "\"Our school library is spacious and bright, with tall wooden shelves full of colorful books.\"", "\"Once there was a farmer who found a magic seed.\""], answer: 2, solution: "1. A descriptive text portrays a thing as it is, in present tense. 2. The library passage describes appearance with adjectives. 3. The others recount events, argue, or narrate a story." },
{ q: "\"Social media harms teenagers' mental health. First, it encourages constant comparison with others. Second, it reduces face-to-face interaction. Therefore, limiting social media use is necessary for teenagers' well-being.\" The thesis is ...", options: ["Therefore, limiting social media use is necessary for teenagers' well-being.", "Social media harms teenagers' mental health.", "First, it encourages constant comparison with others.", "Second, it reduces face-to-face interaction."], answer: 1, solution: "1. The thesis states the writer's position at the start. 2. \"Social media harms teenagers' mental health\" is the claim everything else supports. 3. The other sentences are arguments or the reiteration." },
{ q: "In the same text as the previous question, \"First, it encourages constant comparison with others\" functions as ...", options: ["the thesis", "the reiteration", "an argument", "a recommendation"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Arguments give reasons or evidence supporting the thesis. 2. This sentence gives the first reason why social media harms mental health. 3. It restates nothing and recommends nothing, so it is not thesis, reiteration, or recommendation." },
{ q: "\"In conclusion, homework overload clearly damages students' health and learning quality.\" This sentence functions as ...", options: ["a recommendation", "the reiteration", "a new argument", "the orientation"], answer: 1, solution: "1. A reiteration restates the writer's position to close an analytical exposition. 2. This sentence restates the thesis in different words without adding new reasons. 3. It contains no \"should\" recommendation and no new argument." },
{ q: "Which conjunction shows a cause-effect relationship in analytical exposition?", options: ["however", "for example", "firstly", "because"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Causal conjunctions link a cause to its effect. 2. \"Because\" introduces the reason behind a claim. 3. \"However\" contrasts, \"for example\" exemplifies, and \"firstly\" orders points." },
{ q: "In analytical exposition, the modal \"will\" in \"This trend will continue\" expresses ...", options: ["certainty about the future", "a polite request", "an obligation", "permission"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Analytical expositions persuade with logical certainty. 2. \"Will\" here shows the writer's confidence that the trend continues. 3. It does not request, oblige, or permit anything." },
{ q: "Which text is an analytical exposition?", options: ["\"We should plant more trees. First, turn off your engines. Let us start today.\"", "\"Last year, our village suffered a flood. We evacuated at midnight.\"", "\"Plastic waste pollutes our oceans. It kills marine life and enters our food chain. Thus, reducing plastic use is urgently needed.\"", "\"Some people support zoos, while others oppose them. Both sides have strong reasons.\""], answer: 2, solution: "1. Analytical exposition presents a thesis plus supporting arguments, ending with reiteration. 2. The plastic text argues a position with reasons and closes by restating it. 3. The first recommends action (hortatory), the second recounts, the fourth discusses both sides." },
{ q: "\"Firstly, online learning saves travel time. Secondly, it offers flexible schedules.\" The words \"firstly\" and \"secondly\" are used to ...", options: ["show contrast", "order the arguments", "express cause", "quote a source"], answer: 1, solution: "1. These are enumerative connectives. 2. They list arguments in a clear, numbered order. 3. They neither contrast, show cause, nor cite sources." },
{ q: "The reiteration of an analytical exposition must ...", options: ["introduce a brand-new argument", "give orders to the readers", "tell a short story", "restate the thesis in different words"], answer: 3, solution: "1. \"Reiteration\" literally means restating. 2. Its role is to reinforce the thesis at the end. 3. New arguments, commands, or stories belong to other text parts." },
{ q: "Analytical exposition texts mainly use ...", options: ["the simple present tense", "the simple past tense", "the past perfect tense", "the future continuous tense"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Analytical expositions state general truths and current positions. 2. General truths are expressed in the simple present tense. 3. Past tenses would turn arguments into stories of finished events." },
{ q: "\"It is obvious that deforestation causes floods.\" The phrase \"It is obvious that\" shows the writer's ...", options: ["doubt", "polite request", "strong stance", "neutral report"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Analytical writers take a clear position to persuade. 2. \"It is obvious that\" signals strong conviction in the claim. 3. It shows no doubt, request, or neutrality." },
{ q: "\"Air pollution rises because factories release smoke without filters. As a result, city residents suffer respiratory diseases.\" The causal conjunctions are ...", options: ["rises - suffer", "because - as a result", "without - city", "factories - residents"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Causal conjunctions connect causes and effects. 2. \"Because\" introduces the cause; \"as a result\" introduces the effect. 3. The other pairs are verbs, prepositions, or nouns, not conjunctions." },
{ q: "\"Reading novels improves vocabulary. A 2023 study found that students who read daily scored higher on word tests.\" The second sentence functions as ...", options: ["the thesis", "the reiteration", "a recommendation", "evidence supporting the argument"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Arguments become convincing when backed by facts. 2. The study result is data proving the claim about vocabulary. 3. It is neither the opening claim, the closing restatement, nor a suggestion." },
{ q: "Which sentence best states a thesis for an analytical exposition on electric cars?", options: ["Electric cars are the most practical solution to urban air pollution.", "First, buy an electric car this year.", "I bought an electric car last month.", "Some people like electric cars, but others prefer gasoline cars."], answer: 0, solution: "1. A thesis is a clear, arguable position. 2. This sentence takes a stance that the rest of the text can support with arguments. 3. The second is a command, the third is personal recount, and the fourth presents two sides." },
{ q: "\"Many teenagers sleep too little. Therefore, their concentration at school drops sharply.\" The word \"therefore\" signals ...", options: ["an example", "a contrasting idea", "a conclusion drawn from the previous fact", "a direct quotation"], answer: 2, solution: "1. \"Therefore\" is a causal connective. 2. It shows the second sentence is the logical result of the first. 3. It does not exemplify, contrast, or quote." },
{ q: "The difference between analytical exposition and discussion text is that ...", options: ["analytical exposition tells stories; discussion gives opinions", "analytical exposition argues for one position; discussion presents both pros and cons", "analytical exposition uses past tense; discussion uses future tense", "analytical exposition has no structure; discussion has three parts"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Both are argumentative texts, but their scope differs. 2. Analytical exposition defends a single thesis, while discussion weighs arguments for and against. 3. Both use present tense and have clear structures." },
{ q: "\"Students should bring their own bottles to school. First, it reduces plastic waste. Second, it saves money. In conclusion, let us start this small habit today.\" The thesis is ...", options: ["In conclusion, let us start this small habit today.", "Students should bring their own bottles to school.", "First, it reduces plastic waste.", "Second, it saves money."], answer: 1, solution: "1. A hortatory thesis states what the writer thinks should be done. 2. The opening sentence gives the recommended action. 3. The middle sentences are arguments; the last is the recommendation." },
{ q: "In the same text as the previous question, \"First, it reduces plastic waste\" functions as ...", options: ["the thesis", "the recommendation", "a coda", "an argument"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Arguments support the thesis with reasons. 2. Reducing plastic waste is a reason for bringing own bottles. 3. It is not the opening claim or the closing call to action." },
{ q: "Which sentence is the recommendation?", options: ["Therefore, smokers should quit this dangerous habit now.", "Smoking damages the lungs.", "Smokers spend too much money on cigarettes.", "Many people smoke every day."], answer: 0, solution: "1. A recommendation tells readers what to do, often with \"should\". 2. This sentence urges smokers to quit - a clear call to action. 3. The others state facts without recommending anything." },
{ q: "\"Switch off the lights when you leave the room.\" This sentence uses ...", options: ["a question", "a passive construction", "an imperative", "reported speech"], answer: 2, solution: "1. The sentence starts with the base verb \"switch\" and gives a command. 2. A verb-first command is an imperative sentence. 3. It asks nothing, uses no passive, and reports no speech." },
{ q: "\"Motorcyclists must wear helmets at all times.\" The modal \"must\" expresses ...", options: ["a possibility", "a strong obligation", "a past habit", "an ability"], answer: 1, solution: "1. In hortatory exposition, modals push readers toward action. 2. \"Must\" signals a strong obligation or necessity. 3. It does not mean possibility, ability, or past habit." },
{ q: "A recommendation differs from a reiteration because a recommendation ...", options: ["restates the thesis without new ideas", "tells a moral story", "lists the arguments in order", "calls the readers to take action"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Hortatory texts end by urging action; analytical texts end by restating. 2. A recommendation contains a call like \"should\" or \"let us\". 3. Restating without action is the reiteration's job." },
{ q: "\"Let us keep our rivers clean by never throwing garbage into them.\" The phrase \"let us\" is used to ...", options: ["make a suggestion inviting the readers", "give an order to one person", "ask a question", "report someone's words"], answer: 0, solution: "1. \"Let us\" (let's) proposes a joint action. 2. It invites readers to join the writer in acting. 3. It is softer than a direct order and is not a question or quotation." },
{ q: "Which verb form is used in the imperative \"Save water every day\"?", options: ["the past form of the verb", "the -ing form of the verb", "the base form of the verb", "the third-person singular form"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Imperatives give commands directly. 2. They use the verb's base form with no subject (\"Save\", not \"Saves\"). 3. Past, -ing, and -s forms cannot form imperatives." },
{ q: "Which text is a hortatory exposition?", options: ["\"Waking up early improves focus. Studies show early risers score better. Thus, waking early is clearly beneficial.\"", "\"Everyone should plant a tree this year. Trees clean the air and cool our streets. Join the green movement now.\"", "\"The flood destroyed fifty houses. Volunteers arrived the next morning.\"", "\"Zoos protect endangered species, but they also limit animals' freedom.\""], answer: 1, solution: "1. Hortatory exposition argues that something should (not) be done and ends with a recommendation. 2. The tree text urges action with \"should\" and \"join now\". 3. The first only argues a position, the third recounts, the fourth discusses." },
{ q: "\"Parents should limit children's screen time.\" The modal \"should\" in a hortatory text expresses ...", options: ["a past ability", "a certainty", "a prohibition", "a recommendation"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Hortatory exposition aims to persuade readers to act. 2. \"Should\" here advises parents on what to do - a recommendation. 3. It does not describe ability, certainty, or a ban." },
{ q: "\"The use of smartphones in classrooms has sparked heated debate among teachers and parents.\" This sentence presents the ...", options: ["argument for", "argument against", "issue", "conclusion"], answer: 2, solution: "1. A discussion opens by stating the debatable topic. 2. This sentence introduces the controversy without taking sides. 3. Arguments and conclusions come later." },
{ q: "\"Supporters argue that smartphones give students instant access to learning resources.\" This is ...", options: ["an argument for", "an argument against", "the issue", "a recommendation"], answer: 0, solution: "1. \"Supporters argue\" signals the pro side. 2. Instant access to resources is a benefit - a point for the issue. 3. It is not the opening issue or a final recommendation." },
{ q: "\"Critics, however, claim that phones distract students and open the door to cheating.\" This is ...", options: ["an argument for", "an argument against", "the issue statement", "the thesis"], answer: 1, solution: "1. \"Critics\" signals the opposing side. 2. Distraction and cheating are drawbacks - points against the issue. 3. Discussion texts have no single thesis; they weigh both sides." },
{ q: "\"In conclusion, schools need clear rules so that the benefits of phones outweigh their risks.\" This functions as the ...", options: ["issue", "argument for", "conclusion", "argument against"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Discussion texts close by weighing both sides. 2. This sentence gives a balanced judgment after considering pros and cons. 3. It does not introduce the topic or add a one-sided argument." },
{ q: "\"Online games can sharpen thinking skills. However, excessive gaming harms students' health.\" The word \"however\" is used to ...", options: ["add similar ideas", "give an example", "express cause", "show contrast between the two sides"], answer: 3, solution: "1. \"However\" is a contrastive conjunction. 2. It pivots from a benefit to a drawback - the two sides of the discussion. 3. It does not add, exemplify, or show cause." },
{ q: "\"Electric scooters reduce traffic jams. On the other hand, they cause many accidents on sidewalks.\" The phrase \"on the other hand\" signals ...", options: ["a stronger agreement", "a shift to the opposing viewpoint", "a concluding summary", "a personal story"], answer: 1, solution: "1. This phrase is a classic marker of the \"against\" side. 2. It introduces the contrasting viewpoint after the supporting one. 3. It does not agree, conclude, or narrate." },
{ q: "\"While supporters praise its benefits, opponents question its safety.\" The conjunction \"while\" here shows ...", options: ["contrast between two groups", "time sequence", "cause and effect", "a condition"], answer: 0, solution: "1. \"While\" can join two contrasting clauses. 2. Here it sets supporters' praise against opponents' doubts. 3. No time order, cause, or condition is meant." },
{ q: "Which is an argument FOR school uniforms?", options: ["Uniforms prevent students from expressing their personal style.", "Uniforms cost poor families extra money.", "Uniforms erase visible gaps between rich and poor students.", "Uniforms make students look identical and bored."], answer: 2, solution: "1. An argument \"for\" gives a benefit of the issue. 2. Reducing social gaps is a positive effect of uniforms. 3. The others list drawbacks - arguments against." },
{ q: "The correct generic structure of a discussion text is ...", options: ["orientation - complication - resolution", "thesis - arguments - reiteration", "identification - description", "issue - arguments for and against - conclusion"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Each text type has a fixed structure. 2. Discussion moves from the issue, through both sides' arguments, to a balanced conclusion. 3. The other sequences belong to narrative, analytical exposition, and descriptive texts." },
{ q: "A discussion text differs from an analytical exposition because it ...", options: ["uses only the past tense", "presents both supporting and opposing arguments", "never states any opinion", "tells a fictional story"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Analytical exposition defends one position; discussion stays balanced. 2. Presenting both pros and cons is the defining trait of discussion. 3. Both use present tense and express reasoned views, not fiction." },
{ q: "\"A 5.2-magnitude earthquake struck the coastal town of Pacitan early Tuesday morning, damaging dozens of houses.\" This paragraph is the ...", options: ["background event", "newsworthy event", "source", "headline"], answer: 1, solution: "1. News items open with the main event. 2. This paragraph reports what happened - the core news. 3. Background gives context and sources give quotes; neither is the main event itself." },
{ q: "\"Pacitan sits on an active fault line that has produced three quakes in the past decade.\" This sentence gives ...", options: ["the newsworthy event", "a direct quotation", "the reporter's personal comment", "background information"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Background events give context that helps readers understand the news. 2. The fault-line history explains why the quake happened there. 3. It is not the main event, a quote, or an opinion." },
{ q: "\"'We felt a strong jolt and ran outside immediately,' said Rina, a 34-year-old resident.\" This sentence functions as a ...", options: ["source", "background event", "newsworthy event", "headline"], answer: 0, solution: "1. News items support facts with statements from witnesses or officials. 2. Rina's quoted words are an eyewitness source. 3. She is not the event itself or its background." },
{ q: "\"A landslide buried three houses in the village,\" the reporter wrote. This lead mainly answers ...", options: ["why it happened", "how it happened", "what happened", "what will happen next"], answer: 2, solution: "1. The lead (opening) of a news item summarizes the core event. 2. This sentence states the event itself - what happened. 3. It gives no cause, process, or prediction." },
{ q: "News items mainly use the past tense because they ...", options: ["predict future events", "report events that already happened", "give step-by-step instructions", "describe timeless truths"], answer: 1, solution: "1. News reports real incidents. 2. The incidents occurred before the report was written, so past tense is natural. 3. Prediction, instruction, and general truth belong to other text types." },
{ q: "Direct speech: \"The mayor said, 'We will rebuild the bridge soon.'\" The correct reported-speech version for a news item is ...", options: ["The mayor says that they will rebuild the bridge soon.", "The mayor said, 'They would rebuild the bridge soon.'", "The mayor will say that they rebuilt the bridge soon.", "The mayor said that they would rebuild the bridge soon."], answer: 3, solution: "1. In reported speech, a past reporting verb shifts the quoted verb back. 2. \"Said\" plus \"will\" becomes \"said that ... would\", and \"we\" becomes \"they\". 3. Keeping \"will\" with past \"said\" breaks the tense-shift rule." },
{ q: "Which text is a news item rather than a recount?", options: ["\"Yesterday I visited my grandmother and we baked cookies together.\"", "\"A fire broke out at the central market last night. Two shops were destroyed. The fire chief said the cause is under investigation.\"", "\"Once upon a time, a turtle challenged a rabbit to a race.\"", "\"First, plug in the charger. Then, wait until the battery is full.\""], answer: 1, solution: "1. News items report recent public events with sources. 2. The fire report covers a newsworthy event and quotes an official source. 3. The others are personal recount, fable, and procedure." },
{ q: "The lead paragraph of a news item should ...", options: ["summarize the most important facts of the event", "list all background details", "quote three different sources", "give the reporter's personal opinion"], answer: 0, solution: "1. The lead answers the key 5W+1H questions at a glance. 2. It summarizes who, what, when, and where in one or two sentences. 3. Details, multiple quotes, and opinions come later or not at all." },
{ q: "\"Twelve passengers were rescued by the search team at dawn.\" The passive voice is common in news items because it ...", options: ["hides who performed the action", "makes sentences shorter", "emphasizes the receiver of the action", "avoids using past tense"], answer: 2, solution: "1. In this sentence the focus is the rescued passengers. 2. Passive construction puts the affected people first, which news values. 3. The actor is still named (\"by the search team\"), so nothing is hidden." },
{ q: "\"According to the police, the accident was caused by brake failure.\" The phrase \"according to the police\" shows ...", options: ["the reporter's guess", "source attribution", "a background event", "a headline"], answer: 1, solution: "1. News must show where information comes from. 2. \"According to\" names the authority behind the claim - the source. 3. It is not a guess, background, or headline." },
{ q: "In academic writing, the informal word \"get\" in \"We got good results\" is best replaced with ...", options: ["grab", "fetch", "obtain", "gain up"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Academic style prefers formal, precise verbs. 2. \"Obtain\" is the formal equivalent of \"get\" for results. 3. \"Grab\" and \"fetch\" are informal; \"gain up\" is not a standard collocation." },
{ q: "\"The discovery had a significant impact on medicine.\" In this context, \"significant\" is closest in meaning to ...", options: ["important", "small", "famous", "strange"], answer: 0, solution: "1. \"Significant\" describes the size of the impact. 2. An impact described as significant is major or important. 3. It does not mean small, famous, or strange." },
{ q: "\"The experiment demonstrates that plants grow faster with music.\" The word \"demonstrates\" is closest in meaning to ...", options: ["hides", "guesses", "forgets", "shows clearly"], answer: 3, solution: "1. \"Demonstrate\" in academic contexts means to prove or make clear. 2. The experiment makes the finding clear - it shows it clearly. 3. The other options reverse or miss the meaning." },
{ q: "Choose the correct collocation with the word \"research\"." , options: ["make research", "conduct research", "do a conclusion", "take an experiment"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Collocations are word pairs that naturally go together. 2. \"Conduct research\" is the standard academic pairing. 3. \"Make research\", \"do a conclusion\", and \"take an experiment\" are unnatural in English." },
{ q: "In \"unreliable data\", the prefix \"un-\" means ...", options: ["again", "very", "not", "before"], answer: 2, solution: "1. Prefixes change a word's meaning. 2. \"Un-\" negates the adjective: unreliable = not reliable. 3. \"Again\" is \"re-\", \"before\" is \"pre-\", and \"very\" is not a prefix meaning." },
{ q: "From the verb \"inform\", the correct noun form is ...", options: ["information", "informment", "informal", "informous"], answer: 0, solution: "1. The suffix \"-tion\" turns verbs into nouns. 2. \"Inform\" plus \"-ation\" gives \"information\", the standard noun. 3. The other forms are adjectives or non-words." },
{ q: "Which word is the most formal choice for academic writing?", options: ["buy", "get", "grab", "purchase"], answer: 3, solution: "1. Academic writing avoids casual everyday words. 2. \"Purchase\" is the formal-register equivalent of \"buy\". 3. \"Buy\", \"get\", and \"grab\" are informal." },
{ q: "\"The results were surprising. ___, the method needs improvement.\" The most formal connective is ...", options: ["But", "However", "And", "So"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Academic writing prefers formal sentence connectives. 2. \"However\" is the formal contrastive link between sentences. 3. \"But\", \"and\", and \"so\" are too casual to start sentences in formal prose." },
{ q: "Choose the correct collocation with the word \"conclusion\"." , options: ["take a conclusion", "bring a conclusion", "draw a conclusion", "catch a conclusion"], answer: 2, solution: "1. \"Conclusion\" pairs with a specific verb in English. 2. The fixed collocation is \"draw a conclusion\". 3. The other verbs do not naturally pair with \"conclusion\"." },
{ q: "In the sentence \"The study revealed an enormous gap in funding\", \"enormous\" could be replaced with the more formal ...", options: ["substantial", "huge", "big", "gigantic"], answer: 0, solution: "1. Academic style favors precise Latinate adjectives. 2. \"Substantial\" is the formal academic equivalent meaning large in amount. 3. \"Huge\", \"big\", and \"gigantic\" are informal or journalistic." },
{ q: "In \"rewrite the essay\", the prefix \"re-\" means ...", options: ["not", "before", "against", "again"], answer: 3, solution: "1. \"Re-\" is a common academic prefix. 2. \"Rewrite\" means to write again. 3. \"Not\" is \"un-/in-\", \"before\" is \"pre-\", \"against\" is \"anti-\"." },
{ q: "Choose the correct collocation with the word \"results\"." , options: ["win results", "obtain results", "catch results", "bring results"], answer: 1, solution: "1. Academic verbs pair with \"results\" in fixed ways. 2. \"Obtain results\" is the standard formal collocation. 3. \"Win\", \"catch\", and \"bring\" do not collocate with \"results\"." },
{ q: "\"Clean water is crucial for public health.\" The word \"crucial\" is closest in meaning to ...", options: ["optional", "difficult", "vital", "expensive"], answer: 2, solution: "1. \"Crucial\" describes something decisive or essential. 2. \"Vital\" is its closest synonym - absolutely necessary. 3. It does not mean optional, difficult, or expensive." },
{ q: "\"The new policy will ___ the local economy.\" Choose the correct word.", options: ["affect", "effect", "affects to", "effecting"], answer: 0, solution: "1. \"Affect\" is the verb meaning to influence; \"effect\" is usually the noun. 2. The sentence needs a verb after \"will\", so \"affect\" fits. 3. \"Affects to\" and \"effecting\" are grammatically wrong here." },
{ q: "From the verb \"read\", the adjective \"readable\" means ...", options: ["reading again", "able to be read easily", "not reading", "reading quickly"], answer: 1, solution: "1. The suffix \"-able\" means \"capable of\". 2. \"Readable\" means able to be read (easily or legibly). 3. The other options describe repetition, negation, or speed, not capability." }

  ]
};
